22913206,imgsize-29878.cms"/></item><item><title>‘Never’: Trump denies being told his name was in Epstein files; downplays case as ‘not a big thing’</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/122912981.cms" /&gt;Donald Trump denied being briefed about his name appearing in Jeffrey Epstein's files, contradicting a Wall Street Journal report. He dismissed questions about Ghislaine Maxwell's interview and a potential pardon, stating it's not the right time. Trump shifted focus to others associated with Epstein, accusing the media of exaggerating his involvement.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/never-trump-denies-being-told-his-name-was-in-epstein-files-downplays-case-as-not-a-big-thing/articleshow/122912981.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/never-trump-denies-being-told-his-name-was-in-epstein-files-downplays-case-as-not-a-big-thing/articleshow/122912981.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-26T02:32:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-122912982,imgsize-56612.cms"/></item><item><title>'100 different people': Ghislaine Maxwell gives DOJ exclusive information on Epstein, expects to be pardoned</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/122912925.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/100-different-people-ghislaine-maxwell-gives-doj-exclusive-information-on-epstein-expects-to-be-pardoned/articleshow/122912925.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/100-different-people-ghislaine-maxwell-gives-doj-exclusive-information-on-epstein-expects-to-be-pardoned/articleshow/122912925.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-26T01:57:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-122912931,imgsize-31692.cms"/></item><item><title>Brain in a box: Philadelphia couple sues funeral homes; say dead son’s brain handed over as remains</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/122912399.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/brain-in-a-box-philadelphia-couple-sues-funeral-homes-say-dead-sons-brain-handed-over-as-remains/articleshow/122912399.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/brain-in-a-box-philadelphia-couple-sues-funeral-homes-say-dead-sons-brain-handed-over-as-remains/articleshow/122912399.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-26T01:42:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-122912678,imgsize-23746.cms"/></item><item><title>What's thrifting like in UAE? Is secondhand shopping catching on in a country known for luxury?</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/122909648.cms" /&gt;The UAE’s luxury image is shifting as secondhand shopping gains momentum. Driven by sustainability concerns and changing consumer habits, preloved fashion and goods, from designer clothes to vintage furniture, are becoming increasingly popular. This growing thrift culture reflects a broader movement toward conscious consumption, blending affordability with style and ethics, signaling a significant transformation in the region’s retail landscape.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/whats-thrifting-like-in-uae-is-secondhand-shopping-catching-on-in-a-country-known-for-luxury/articleshow/122909648.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/whats-thrifting-like-in-uae-is-secondhand-shopping-catching-on-in-a-country-known-for-luxury/articleshow/122909648.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-26T01:27:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-122912814,imgsize-1561016.cms"/></item><item><title>'Chuck E, come with me': Pizza outlet mascot arrested in Florida; charged with credit card fraud</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/122911414.cms" /&gt;A Chuck E. Cheese mascot, Jermel Jones, was arrested in Tallahassee, Florida, while in costume. Police apprehended Jones after a customer, Michelle Allen, reported fraudulent charges on her credit card following a birthday party at the restaurant. Authorities found Allen's Visa card and a related receipt in Jones' possession, leading to charges of larceny and fraudulent card use.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chuck-e-come-with-me-pizza-outlet-mascot-arrested-in-florida-charged-with-credit-card-fraud/articleshow/122911414.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chuck-e-come-with-me-pizza-outlet-mascot-arrested-in-florida-charged-with-credit-card-fraud/articleshow/122911414.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-07-26T01:02:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-122911497,imgsize-1247186.cms"/></item><item><title>Outrage in China as thousands of private pictures of girls posted online</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/122912502.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofi